# GEMINI API CONFIGURATION (server-side only)
# Get your API key from: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# NO VITE_ PREFIX: this key is read only by the serverless function api/gemini.ts
# (process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY). With VITE_ it would be embedded in the public bundle.
# In production it lives in Vercel → Project Settings → Environment Variables.
# Locally it is only used when running the api/ functions (e.g. `vercel dev`);
# plain `npm run dev` does not serve /api/gemini.
GEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY_HERE

# IMPORTANT NOTES:
# - Only browser-side variables use the VITE_ prefix (Supabase URL + anon key).
#   Never put a secret behind VITE_: everything with that prefix ends up in the bundle.
# - DO NOT commit the actual .env file to git (it's in .gitignore)
# - In Vercel, add these variables in: Project Settings → Environment Variables
